			"date": "2025-10-29T13:47:11.000Z",
			"content": "I think <a href=\"https://webawesome.com/docs/components/copy-button/#dependencies\">webawesome.com/docs/compone...</a> and <a href=\"https://webawesome.com/docs/#the-difference-between-dist-and-dist-cdn\">webawesome.com/docs/#the-di...</a> are probably the relevant parts of the docs for that question (but on the 11ty implementation we bundle to a single file, as noted in the blog post)",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1950937,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mstdn.social/@scottjehl/115463830334101521",
			"author": {
				"name": "Scott Jehl",
				"url": "https://mstdn.social/@scottjehl",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/11a7482b10dafe56809db4c39a89431dee6d55225dd4ac6bec19886f8fa40b94.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-30T15:30:31.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@mia\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>mia</span></a></span> and exceptions to this make sense too. <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span>'s post highlights a good example of an empty custom element use-case. I think anyway. But I wouldn't want to use them for core functionality <a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/copy-paste/\"><span>https://www.</span><span>zachleat.com/web/copy-paste/</span><span></span></a></p>\n<a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/copy-paste/\">Copy *and* Paste? …in this Economy?—zachleat.com</a>",
